  <sys:String x:Key="preset.gamer.name">Gamer Mode</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="preset.gamer.desc">One bundle: Game Mode, Game Bar/DVR off, power plan, MMCSS, visual simplification, telemetry reduction, SysMain off, and similar tweaks.&#x0a;For: Gaming PCs. Read the preview list first, then apply.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="preset.balanced.name">Balanced Mode</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="preset.balanced.desc">Light touch: Game Mode plus basic privacy. No aggressive service shutdown.&#x0a;For: &quot;I want a little optimization but do not want to break Windows&quot;.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="preset.minimal.name">Minimal / Server Mode</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="preset.minimal.desc">As lean as possible: telemetry, animations, background apps, unneeded services…&#x0a;For: Second PC, HTPC, or &quot;just get work done&quot; machines. Try Gamer first on your main gaming PC.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="preset.laptop.name">Laptop / Battery Mode</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="preset.laptop.desc">Skips aggressive gaming power tweaks (Ultimate Performance, core parking off); focuses on telemetry reduction, visual simplification, and background-app limits — a balanced laptop profile.&#x0a;For: Notebooks where battery life matters.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="preset.privacymax.name">Maximum Privacy</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="preset.privacymax.desc">More aggressive than Balanced, but not as service-heavy as Minimal: applies telemetry, location, advertising ID, and personalization tweaks together in one privacy-focused profile.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="preset.defaults.name">Restore Defaults (Undo Session)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="preset.defaults.desc">Reverts reversible changes from this WinCleaner session (Undo All).&#x0a;Note: Removed apps do not come back — reinstall those from the Store.</sys:String>
